# AGENT.md — src/infrastructure/

Adapters. Everything that talks to the outside world lives here.

## Rules

- May import from `application/` and `domain/`. Nothing in those layers may
  import from here — enforce this direction in every change.
- Repository implementations must satisfy the interface declared in
  `domain/<module>/repositories/`. If the interface does not fit, change the
  interface deliberately; do not widen the implementation and cast.
- Controllers stay thin: parse, delegate to a use-case, return. No business
  logic, no direct repository access.
- Database rows are not domain entities. Map explicitly at this boundary.

## What goes where

- `<module>/controllers/` — HTTP entry points.
- `<module>/persistence/` — repository implementations{{#if ormTypeorm}} and the
  TypeORM `*.orm-entity.ts` persistence models{{/if}}{{#if ormMongoose}} and the
  Mongoose `*.schema.ts` persistence models{{/if}}.
- `<module>/<module>.module.ts` — DI wiring. This is where the concrete
  repository is bound to the domain's token; swapping data layers is a
  one-line change here.
